<Project Version="4" Seed="1">
	<Description>The neat OR: input B delayed by 30 degrees, so a quarter of the total reaches Q with both on, the same level as for A or B alone. The fibres start 75 px apart (gap 63 px), S-bend over 228 px to a gap of 15 px, run parallel for 437 px and bend apart again. 0.7856 rad of coupling phase (the straight run's kappa 0.001487 rad/px times 437 px plus 0.0678 rad for each bend); one coupling length at this gap is 1056.1 px. Source B at -30 degrees. Wavelength 32.04 px in vacuum, 17.80 px in the core (index 1.8) and 22.89 px in the medium (index 1.4); single-mode core 12 px wide, beta 0.3223 rad/px, evanescent decay length 5.92 px.
Coupler: 0.7856 rad</Description>
